## Findings log
G1 (Seam Map) Risklytics = existing startup: AI platform analysing insurance policies, filings, AI liability gaps; tracks forms/endorsements/filings; founder Samuel Gold. https://datainnovation.org/2026/07/5-qs-with-samuel-gold-founder-of-risklytics/ (no funding data found). Fenwick already tells policyholders to do comprehensive policy reviews + DIC/captive/manuscript endorsements. No Marsh/Aon/WTW AI-exclusion tool found by search (negative; brokers do this bundled free). Bloomberg/Haynes Boone/Fenwick: renewal negotiation advice is free commentary.
G2 (Warranty File) Travelers v ICS: voluntarily dismissed 2022-08-26, policy stipulated rescinded after loss (insideprivacy/Reed Smith). Columbia Casualty v Cottage Health = negligent misrep argument. Verification startups exist: IntellectAI Risk Analyst (checks submissions vs outside signals), Coalition continuous scan, Cyberwrite, SecondSight/INSUREtrust Cyber Pre-Check. Marsh stat 41% of cyber apps denied on first submission (secondary, unverified). No incontestability endorsement for cyber found.
G3 (Mutual) Lawfare article (Trout, Kvist, Dattani) = ADVOCACY for frontier AI mutual "AIMIL" (Kvist is AIUC CEO; AIUC is therefore positioned to build it). No lab captive/mutual found. https://www.lawfaremedia.org/article/bootstrapping-frontier-ai-governance-by-mutualizing-risk . CrowdStrike Project QuiltWorks (May 28 2026) = insurers (Coalition, Liberty Mutual, Lockton, Resilience, Marsh) financing frontier AI cyber risk.
